ProsperoSunshine: tell the platform whose input it passes on

The PS5 host gives each paired device the console profiles it may play as. Such a device plays through its controllers
(or its keyboard's own pad) as those profiles. Its keyboard and mouse would still reach the console's shared keyboard and
mouse, which belong to no profile the host chose: with more than one profile signed in, the console asks who uses them,
and whoever answers picks any profile.

passthrough_next_message() now tells the platform, through the new platf::set_input_owner, which session's input it
passes on, by the session's feedback queue (the one platf::set_gamepad_owner was given), and clears it afterwards. The
PS5 platform drops the shared keyboard and mouse input of a device with its own profiles.

--- a/src/platform/common.h
+++ b/src/platform/common.h
@@ -1315,6 +1315,14 @@
    */
   void set_gamepad_owner(const feedback_queue_t &feedback_queue, std::string_view owner);
   /**
+   * @brief Tell the platform whose input the calling thread passes on next.
+   *
+   * The PS5 host keeps the console's shared keyboard and mouse from a device that may only watch.
+   *
+   * @param feedback_queue The session's feedback queue, as set_gamepad_owner was given it; null once done.
+   */
+  void set_input_owner(const feedback_queue_t *feedback_queue);
+  /**
    * @brief Release gamepad resources.
    *
    * @param input Platform input backend that receives the event.
--- a/src/input.cpp
+++ b/src/input.cpp
@@ -2548,6 +2548,7 @@
 #endif
 
     // Send the batched input to the OS
+    platf::set_input_owner(&input->feedback_queue);
     switch (util::endian::little(payload->magic)) {
       case MOUSE_MOVE_REL_MAGIC_GEN5:
         passthrough(input, (PNV_REL_MOUSE_MOVE_PACKET) payload);
@@ -2594,6 +2595,7 @@
         passthrough(input, (PSS_CONTROLLER_BATTERY_PACKET) payload);
         break;
     }
+    platf::set_input_owner(nullptr);
     return true;
   }
 
